{"name":"Aqua Blue","hex":"#79b6bc","fetched":"2026-11-01","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"aqua","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Water (as a compound).","A shade of colour, usually a mix of blue and green, most often similar to the colour cyan, though also sometimes closer to turquoise or aquamarine."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a greenish-blue colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aqua"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aqua Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Aqua Blue is a conventional passenger-roaming ship of the Seajets company. It is considered one of the most recognizable ships of the Greek coastal shipping fleet, as it has been serving for almost three decades in Greek seas, after an extensive renovation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/%CE%95%CF%80%CE%B9%CE%B2%CE%B1%CF%84%CE%B7%CE%B3%CF%8C_%CF%80%CE%BB%CE%BF%CE%AF%CE%BF.jpg/330px-%CE%95%CF%80%CE%B9%CE%B2%CE%B1%CF%84%CE%B7%CE%B3%CF%8C_%CF%80%CE%BB%CE%BF%CE%AF%CE%BF.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aqua_Blue","wikidata":"Q24863496"},{"title":"Aqua (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Aqua is a variation of the color cyan. The normalized color coordinates for the two web colors named aqua and cyan are identical. It was one of the three secondary colors of the RGB color model used on computer and television displays. In the HSV color wheel aqua is precisely halfway between blue and green. However, aqua is not the same as the primary subtractive color named process cyan used in printing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Shaheed_Island%2C_Andamans%2C_Bay%2C_Turquoise_water.jpg/330px-Shaheed_Island%2C_Andamans%2C_Bay%2C_Turquoise_water.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aqua_(color)","wikidata":"Q372733"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/%CE%95%CF%80%CE%B9%CE%B2%CE%B1%CF%84%CE%B7%CE%B3%CF%8C_%CF%80%CE%BB%CE%BF%CE%AF%CE%BF.jpg/500px-%CE%95%CF%80%CE%B9%CE%B2%CE%B1%CF%84%CE%B7%CE%B3%CF%8C_%CF%80%CE%BB%CE%BF%CE%AF%CE%BF.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/%CE%95%CF%80%CE%B9%CE%B2%CE%B1%CF%84%CE%B7%CE%B3%CF%8C_%CF%80%CE%BB%CE%BF%CE%AF%CE%BF.jpg/500px-%CE%95%CF%80%CE%B9%CE%B2%CE%B1%CF%84%CE%B7%CE%B3%CF%8C_%CF%80%CE%BB%CE%BF%CE%AF%CE%BF.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.